              "date": "2026-08-04T07:16:18Z"
            }
          ],
          "series_items": [],
          "patch_summary": "This patch modifies the tracing of lock contention events in Linux by using a new macro, TRACE_EVENT_FN(), for the contended_release event. This change allows for more flexibility and customization when tracing this specific event. The patch introduces weak no-op hooks for architectures to override if they need custom behavior. Currently, these hooks are empty, resulting in no functional changes until an architecture overrides them.",
          "analysis_source": "llm-chunked-no-replies",
