              "message_id": "b8daabae6469ad72cc784a911f6cc43a6d45df3a.1785778551.git.d@ilvokhin.com",
              "url": "https://lore.kernel.org/all/b8daabae6469ad72cc784a911f6cc43a6d45df3a.1785778551.git.d@ilvokhin.com/",
              "subject": "[PATCH 2/5] locking: Factor out queued_spin_release()",
              "date": "2026-08-04T07:16:17Z"
            }
          ],
          "series_items": [],
          "patch_summary": "This patch introduces a new function, queued_spin_release(), which is an arch-overridable release primitive for spinlocks. It creates a generic wrapper around the existing queued_spin_unlock() function, allowing architectures to customize only the release behavior if needed. The MIPS architecture's override is renamed to match this change, but x86 paravirt remains unchanged as it directly overrides queued_spin_unlock(). This patch does not introduce any functional changes and is intended to facilitate future tracing and debugging efforts.",
          "analysis_source": "llm-chunked-no-replies",
          "review_comments": [],
          "list_id": "kvm@vger.kernel.org"
        },
