              "date": "2026-08-04T07:16:17Z"
            }
          ],
          "series_items": [],
          "patch_summary": "This patch replaces the use of paravirt-ops ALTERNATIVE machinery for dispatching spinlock operations on x86 architecture with static_call(). This change allows the target function to be updated at runtime, which is necessary for implementing a contended_release tracepoint. The patch updates several files in the kernel and includes changes to support module safety and boot testing on native and KVM PV guest systems.",
          "analysis_source": "llm-per-reviewer",
          "review_comments": [
            {
              "author": "Borislav Petkov",
              "summary": "Reviewer Petkov suggested redefining X86_FEATURE_PVUNLOCK to a static value, allowing for easier reuse of the feature flag.",
              "sentiment": "NEUTRAL",
              "sentiment_signals": [
                "suggested improvement"
              ],
              "has_inline_review": true,
              "tags_given": [
                "Reviewed-by"
              ],
              "raw_body": "No, do:\n\n/* free: was #define X86_FEATURE_PVUNLOCK\t\t( 8*32+20) /* PV unlock function */\n\nso that we can reuse it by finding it easier.",
